# Intake: the only thing on a timer. Token-free on a quiet tick.
# Anything it prints is an escalation, so whatever reads cron mail is your alert channel.
#
# Install with:  sudo crontab -u partyline -e    (paste the line below)
# Add MAILTO=you@example.com at the top to get the escalations by mail.

* * * * * . /etc/partyline/config.env && /usr/bin/python3 /opt/partyline/intake/collect.py

# Notes
#  * one minute, not five: the poll is cheap, and latency is what your peer notices
#  * the collector takes a flock, so a slow tick cannot overlap the next one
#  * keep it no_agent (a script). Never let the poll become a model call.
